WHAT THE PATCH DOES (introspection only; it tunes nothing):

1. vllm/v1/engine/core.py — EngineCore._initialize_kv_caches, immediately after
   the scheduler KV cache config is final (num_gpu_blocks set, global
   block_size resolved, the "GPU KV cache size" line printed) and before the
   workers allocate: emit one "kv-allocation-plan/v1" JSON record per engine.
   Channels, in priority order for a capture route:
     a. one startup log line:  KV_ALLOCATION_PLAN_JSON <compact-json>
     b. if VLLM_KV_ALLOCATION_PLAN_PATH is set: the identical canonical line
        (sort_keys, compact separators, trailing newline) written via tmp file
        + os.replace, best-effort, never fatal.
   The record carries: the runtime self-report (vllm.__version__, whose
   trailing +g<sha> names the source revision), an optional deployment-supplied
   image digest (VLLM_KV_ALLOCATION_PLAN_IMAGE_DIGEST; a self-report beside the
   observer's authoritative launch reading), the resolved cache format
   (cache_config.cache_dtype), allocator_blocks (scheduler num_blocks),
   requested_length (max_model_len), scheduler_block_size, per-group rows
   (identity, upstream spec kind, layer identities, block size, page size
   bytes, tokens per state, sliding window, max memory usage bytes, blocks at
   the requested length), and a grouping/padding statement quoted from the
   resolved spec fields (group count, rostered layer count, per-layer
   page-size padding notes).
   Per-group figures are read through the engine's own spec methods:
   max_memory_usage_bytes(vllm_config) at max_model_len and
   cdiv(usage, page_size_bytes) — the exact arithmetic of
   get_max_concurrency_for_kv_cache_config — so the emission reproduces the
   printed capacity by construction, which is the independent control the
   corpus-side mint (extdeps.vllm.kv_layout ResolvedKvAllocationPlan) checks.
   tokens_per_state normalizes the mamba sentinel (-1, a not-token-keyed
   recurrent state) to 1, matching get_num_kernel_states' one-state-per-block
   charge.
2. vllm/envs.py — declares the two environment variables.

Emission point chosen over EngineCore.get_kv_cache_group_metadata (the
corpus's named surface for today's emission): that method is a lazy query
returning kind/block_size/sliding_window only, and it runs after the
scheduler exists; the allocation plan is COMPLETE at the end of
_initialize_kv_caches, in the head EngineCore process, on every code path
that prints the capacity line. The head/rank split is survived by tagging the
record with engine_dp_rank and by the fact that only the engine that printed
the capacity line is the control's subject; a capture route binds the
dp_rank 0 record.

